[h1]Phobos Medical[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.5.2
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - held draft, awaiting owner gameplay checks

Halewright's Ward-3 gives injured and unconscious crew a place to recuperate; the Vigil-2 keeps the watch informed. Both now have descriptions in their maker's voice, with their limits explicit.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Lay patient here[/b]: drag an unconscious crew member to the bed and right-click it. They lie down and start recuperating.
[*][b]Rest and recover[/b]: an injured crew member lies down awake and recuperates without being tired. They fall asleep in place if sleepy and get up once their injuries have eased.
[*][b]Sleep[/b]: anyone tired may sleep in a free Ward-3, as in the vanilla bed, unless you keep it for the injured.
[*]While the bed has power and air, its patient gets the game's own medical-rest healing, the same as the vanilla Infirmaway gives a sleeper. Cut the power and the care stops, with one line in the crew log, until it returns.
[*][b]Send injured crew here[/b]: switch it on and a free bed calls the worst-off injured crew member to rest, without cancelling what they are doing.
[*][b]Weightless care[/b]: weightlessness normally slows wound healing to a twentieth; under the Ward-3's care a patient heals at the normal rate.
[*]A Control Panel shows the patient, how long they have been under care, blood lost, infection, pain, the worst wound and any bleeding.
[*][b]Vigil-2 patient monitor[/b]: stand it beside the bed for the patient's blood loss, infection, pain and every wound, with the change over the last hour, and a caution in the crew log when something gets worse. It only watches. With Inspection rounds on, idle crew check the bed and monitor daily.
[*][b]Keep patient treated[/b]: switch it on and the crew dress bleeding wounds, splint broken bones and change dirty dressings on whoever lies in the bed, worst first, using cloth and splints from its drawer and fetching more from around the ship. Crew with the trauma or nursing skill go first and work faster.
[*]A small bedside drawer for dressings, splints and medicines.
[/list]

[h2]Tune it yourself[/h2]
The bed's power, the thresholds that decide who counts as injured and the treatments the crew give live in a data file. You can add a treatment of your own. Drop your own file in BepInEx/config/PhobosMedical/care to change them; a bad file is skipped with a message, never half-applied. The healing stays the game's own.

[h2]Getting started[/h2]
[list]
[*]Buy a Ward-3 at the K-Leg furnishings kiosk (or a worn or broken one elsewhere) and install it through INSTALL, FURN with its head against a wall carrying power.
[*]Right-click it for Rest and recover, Sleep, Lay patient here, Keep patient treated and its Control Panel.
[*]In the F3 console, phobosmedical list shows the beds on your ship.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.127.2 or newer.
[*]BepInEx 5 through EddieSM / EsMM27's [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3741030124]BepInEx Mod Loader[/url], including its one-time setup.
[/list]

[h2]Installing from the Workshop[/h2]
[list]
[*]Subscribe to the BepInEx Mod Loader and follow its setup instructions.
[*]Subscribe to Phobos Medical and the Phobos items listed under Required items.
[*]Start Ostranauts once so the loader copies the plugins, then restart it once so they load. Do the same after each update.
[*]Check that the mods are enabled in the MODS screen.
[/list]

[h2]Saves and limits[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ordinary saves are supported. Each bed remembers its patient and setting.
[*]Its cartridges and folded arms are styling for a 2075 sickbay; the healing is the game's own medical rest, not nanomachine surgery.
[*]The crew treat with the game's own cloth and splints; there are no pills, disinfection or surgery. An autodoc is planned.
[*]Automated checks pass; in-game checks are still pending.
[/list]

[h2]Credits[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games or Kitfox Games. It uses the game's own sleep, recuperation, wound and drag systems.

The matching Phobos cover shows a spacer resting in the Ward-3. It is original promotional artwork made with OpenAI's image tool, rather than a gameplay screenshot; it adds no treatments.

